&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;238&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build the cloud platform that turns Graphcore AI systems into usable, scalable services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;240&quot; data-end=&quot;484&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Graphcore needs a Staff Cloud Engineer to develop and deploy private and public cloud services for AI compute. You will join the Cloud Platform team within Software Platform, close to datacentre operations and product development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;486&quot; data-end=&quot;698&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Your work will shape how internal users and customers access large-scale AI systems. You will keep critical infrastructure available while helping pre-release hardware and software become reliable cloud services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;700&quot; data-end=&quot;956&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You will operate and extend OpenStack-based services, automate deployment with infrastructure-as-code, and improve observability across the fleet. You will benchmark, validate and optimise systems spanning Graphcore hardware, servers, switches and storage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;958&quot; data-end=&quot;1160&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This role suits someone who wants ownership of hard infrastructure problems, not a narrow ticket queue. Expect unproven components, direct user feedbac

&lt;h1 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-section-id=&quot;cxqrzp&quot; data-start=&quot;206&quot; data-end=&quot;221&quot;&gt;About the job&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;223&quot; data-end=&quot;296&quot;&gt;Build the test systems that help deliver AI hardware at production scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;298&quot; data-end=&quot;522&quot;&gt;As a Staff Hardware System Test Engineer, you&#39;ll develop manufacturing test solutions for complex compute systems. Your work will help ensure products reach customers with the quality and reliability expected from Graphcore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;524&quot; data-end=&quot;749&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll shape how hardware is tested across Host Processor Modules, server blades, and multi-node racks. The tools, test content, and diagnostics you create will directly influence manufacturing efficiency and product quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;751&quot; data-end=&quot;978&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll develop test software, design test approaches, and solve challenging hardware issues. You&#39;ll work closely with hardware, firmware, software, and manufacturing teams to improve test coverage and diagnose problems quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;980&quot; data-end=&quot;1236&quot;&gt;This role offers broad technical scope across silicon, boards, systems, software, and manufacturing. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to influence engineering decisions and raise technical standards across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 data-section-id=&quot;80lep1&quot; data-start=&quot;1238&quot; data-end=&quot;1260&quot;&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1262&quot; data-end=&quot;1503&quot;&gt;The Product Test and Diagnosis team owns the strategy for finding and diagnosing hardware defects throughout the product lifecycle. The team works across silicon, boards, servers, and ra

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the test strategy that protects Graphcore’s system software releases at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff System Software Engineer, you will shape integration and system testing across firmware, BMC and Linux device drivers. Your work will help create a high quality gate for system software release packages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, build, automate and report tests across complex server class systems. You will also develop reusable tools, pipelines and packaging solutions that help teams move faster with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role needs deep low level software knowledge and strong system thinking. You will own hard technical areas, guide best practice and stay close to the code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a new integration and system test team within System Software QA. The team verifies integrated components across BMC, firmware and Linux device drivers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work happens close to the hardware, across component teams and QA. You will partner with developers, consult package stakeholders and turn use cases into robust system tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decisions are shaped by evidence, clear technical reasoning and ownership. You will be expected to speak up, act fast and raise standards through hands-on leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Strong experience in low level system testing and integration across complex software and hardware layers.&lt;br&gt;· Deep understanding of RTOS, complex boot logic, Linux and device drivers.&lt;br&gt;· Test development capability using Python and C/C++.&lt;br&gt;· Experience working with hardware, debuggers, CI/CD pipelines and build or integration tools.&lt;br&gt;· Ability to

&lt;div class=&quot;description content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solution architect for Enterprise Modernization in Europe is a senior subject matter expert responsible for technical excellence, solution integrity, and capability development within the service line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This hands-on role leads high-impact client engagements, contributes to pre-sales and solution design, and ensures the regional adoption and evolution of service-specific delivery frameworks, tools, and best practices. The role brings deep expertise in modernization strategies and execution in large legacy systems modernization programs, serving as a trusted technical advisor to both clients and internal teams. This role is key to ensuring delivery quality, enabling service adoption, and evolving the technical maturity of the offering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
